			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">Sriani went outside to get a bit of sun before it faded. As she opened the door, she noticed a large group of her guildmates crowded around Trocair, one of their clerics. Trocair seemed to be holding a packet of paper, and everyone was craning their necks to listen as she read aloud. There were gasps of astonishment, murmurs of anger. Sriani walked up to the group to see what was going on.
<br />

<br />
"Hey guys." She smiled. "What are you doing?"
<br />

<br />
Trocair looked up and shot her a quick smile, and then shook the papers in the air. "This just came in with one of our scouts. Seems it's being passed around the locals, some kind of newspaper."
<br />

<br />
She handed Sriani the paper and everyone waited patiently for her to read it. At last she finished and with a blush of anger on her cheeks, tore the papers up and ground them under her boot into the mud. There were chuckles all around.
<br />

<br />
"That's what I think of this garbage." She sneered, then looked around. "Anyone who beleives any of it can take himself off for a fool. They're trying to get us angry, to make us act irrationally."
<br />

<br />
"It's laughable." Igelei grinned. "She can't even spell."
<br />

<br />
"Or bother to capitalize, use periods or any other grammatical necessities." Jabekez rolled his eyes. 
<br />

<br />
"And those drawings, supposedly of the battles they won?" Oscarvon laughed. "They seem to forget the ever so small detail that they only could win after we left from boredom."
<br />

<br />
"Yeah kicking ass gets tiring." Zefnir nodded. There were more chuckles. The guildmates began to share stories fresh from the front lines.
<br />

<br />
 As their laughter carried to the sky, so did a tiny piece of paper, mud-speckled and torn from the offending newsheet. In printed block writing it said: "Written by: AlouraGrimmLion". And though no one beleive a word of its misspelled fantasy, it was good for a laugh when one was sorely needed.<div style="vertical-align: bottom"><br /><br /><br />_________________<br /><a href="http://www.magelo.com/eq_view_profile.html?num=956867" target="_blank" class="postlink">~Sriani HeartofWolf~</a>
<br />
66 Lady of War
<br />
